  "title": "The field drives learning, then learned skills leave it",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "41a91ab0-471e-4957-88ef-893872e09000",
      "text": "Small conscious pushes from the field guide new motor skills, and through Hebbian synapses repeated field influence hard-wires the network, after which the skill runs without conscious field input. External fields should therefore interfere with memory and learning.",
